---
name: bankan
description: Read and mutate local kanban boards stored as markdown files. Use when the user asks about cards, lanes, boards, or tasks tracked in bankan.
---

## Basics

`{{.Cmd}}` manages local kanban boards stored as plain markdown files.
Board is auto-detected by walking up from cwd; use `--board <dir>` whenever the target board is ambiguous.
Card bodies, board bodies, and comments should be written in **Markdown** when formatting matters.

## Targeting rules

1. If cwd is clearly inside one board, plain `{{.Cmd}} ...` is fine.
2. If the repo may contain multiple boards, always pass `--board <dir>` for board-scoped commands.
3. Use `--root <dir>` only for multi-board commands such as `board reorder`, `board hide`, `board unhide`, and `card search`.
4. `card search` is **ID-only**. It does not search by title or body text.

## Card discovery workflow

1. Establish board context first. If the prompt does not name a board and cwd is ambiguous, inspect the repo and then use `--board <dir>`.
2. Read exact lane names with `{{.Cmd}} lane list`.
3. Discover candidate cards with `{{.Cmd}} card list [--lane <name>] [--label <id>]`.
4. Confirm the exact card with `{{.Cmd}} card show <id>` before mutating it.
5. If the prompt names a card by title/theme instead of ID and `card list` is not enough, use **read-only shell search** (for example `rg`) against board files to find likely cards, then switch back to `{{.Cmd}}` using the discovered card ID.
6. If multiple cards still match, ask the user instead of guessing.

Example read-only fallback:

    rg -n "oauth|login bug|sprint planning" <board-dir>

## Lane

```
{{.Cmd}} lane list
{{.Cmd}} lane add <name>
{{.Cmd}} lane rename <old-name> <new-name>
{{.Cmd}} lane remove <name>               # lane must be empty
```

## Card

```
{{.Cmd}} card list [--lane <name>] [--label <id>] [--archived]
{{.Cmd}} card show <id>                   # title, body, labels, comments
{{.Cmd}} card add  --lane <name> --title "<title>" [--body "<body>"|--body -] [--label <id>]
{{.Cmd}} card edit <id> [--title "<t>"] [--body "<b>"|--body -] [--add-label <id>] [--remove-label <id>] [--primary-label <id>]
{{.Cmd}} card move <id> --lane <name>
{{.Cmd}} card archive <id>
{{.Cmd}} card restore <id> --lane <name>  # un-archive; destination lane required
{{.Cmd}} card delete  <id> [--force]      # omit --force to preview; --force to confirm
{{.Cmd}} card reorder <id> <new-index>    # move within current lane; 0-based index
{{.Cmd}} card duplicate <id>              # copy card in same lane
{{.Cmd}} card search  <id> [--root <dir>] [--include-archived] # find which board(s) contain a card by ID
```

## Comment

```
{{.Cmd}} comment list <card-id>                                    # also shows comment IDs
{{.Cmd}} comment add  <card-id> --text "<text>"|--text - [--author "<name>"]
{{.Cmd}} comment edit <comment-id> --card <card-id> --text "<text>"|--text -
```

## Label

```
{{.Cmd}} label list
{{.Cmd}} label add    --name "<name>" --color "<hex>"
{{.Cmd}} label edit   <id> [--name "<name>"] [--color "<hex>"]
{{.Cmd}} label remove <id> [--force]
```

## Board

```
{{.Cmd}} board init [dir] [--name "<name>"]
{{.Cmd}} board show                              # regular boards and view boards
{{.Cmd}} board reorder --root <dir> <id1> ...   # list all board IDs in desired order
{{.Cmd}} board hide   <id> --root <dir>          # hide board from tab bar
{{.Cmd}} board unhide <id> --root <dir>          # restore board to tab bar
```

## View board

```
{{.Cmd}} board view create <dir> --parent <board-dir> --label <label-id> [--name "<name>"]
{{.Cmd}} board view sync --board <view-board-dir>
{{.Cmd}} board view show --board <view-board-dir>
{{.Cmd}} board view archive --board <view-board-dir> [--archive-label]
```

`board reorder`, `board hide`, and `board unhide` require `--root`.

## Stdin input (IMPORTANT for agents)

Pass `-` as the value to read content from stdin until EOF — **always prefer this for multi-line bodies**:

    echo "# Heading\n\nBody text." | {{.Cmd}} card add --lane <name> --title "<t>" --body -
    echo "My comment"              | {{.Cmd}} comment add <card-id> --text -
    cat description.md             | {{.Cmd}} card edit <id> --body -

## Rules

- Lane names are **case-sensitive** — always read from `lane list` before use.
- `--label` (card add) and `--add-label`/`--remove-label` (card edit) take **label IDs**, not names — get IDs from `label list`.
- `--primary-label` takes a **label ID** too; pass an empty string to clear it.
- Archived cards are hidden from `card list` by default; use `--archived` to see them.
- `card list --archived` is **not valid on view boards**.
- `card restore` is **not available on view boards**.
- On a view board, `card archive` and `card delete --force` remove the filter label from the **parent card** instead of moving/deleting a standalone copy.
- `card delete` without `--force` only prints a preview — add `--force` to delete permanently.
- `card search` scans all active boards (including view boards) under `--root` (default: cwd); archived view boards are skipped by default — use `--include-archived` to include them. Archived cards within active boards are not searched. Prints a warning when the same ID appears in multiple boards.
- `label remove` archives the label by default; use `--force` to permanently delete it.
- On view boards, `label list` shows **parent board labels** and marks the view's filter label.
